<article class="env-definition" id="0175">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0175">Definition <span data-tag="0175">14.11.1</span>.</a> Let $U$ be a simplicial set. We say $x$ is an <em>$n$-simplex of $U$</em> to signify that $x$ is an element of $U_ n$. We say that $y$ is the $j$th <em>face of $x$</em> to signify that $d^ n_ jx = y$. We say that $z$ is the $j$th <em>degeneracy of $x$</em> if $z = s^ n_ jx$. A simplex is called <em>degenerate</em> if it is the degeneracy of another simplex. </p>
</article>